Third-party software and models
-------------------------------

- ONNX Runtime (MIT License), https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  Bundled as a shared library in the triage container images, together with its
  LICENSE and ThirdPartyNotices.txt (/opt/onnxruntime). It is not included in the
  release archives: users of the binary install it separately. Loaded at run time.

- RouteLLM (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/lm-sys/RouteLLM
  The reference inference code is vendored in research/routellm_ref (pinned at
  commit 0b64fdafe049e596a3f5657c219329f24af24198) and is used only for offline
  parity checks and evaluation. Its license applies to that directory.

- dslim/bert-base-NER (MIT License), https://huggingface.co/dslim/bert-base-NER
  Optional English NER model. It is not distributed with Triage; the user
  downloads it with "triage models pull ner". The repository has no LICENSE file;
  the MIT license comes from the model card metadata.

- routellm/bert_gpt4_augmented and routellm/mf_gpt4_augmented (Hugging Face),
  https://huggingface.co/routellm. Not distributed with Triage; the user downloads
  them with "triage models pull bert" and "triage models pull mf". The bert
  repository carries the Apache-2.0 text as LICENSE with the copyright line left
  unfilled ("Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]"), so no copyright holder is
  named. The mf repository has no LICENSE file and no model card; its weights are
  only ever downloaded by the user and are not redistributed by this project.
  Pinned revisions and file hashes: models/manifest.yaml.

- models/bert/graph.onnx, embedded in the triage binary, is a weight-free graph of
  the xlm-roberta-base architecture (Apache-2.0) generated by
  research/src/triage_research/build_bert_graph.py; it contains no trained weights.

- internal/platform/hftok contains Go ports of parts of Hugging Face tokenizers
  (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers.

- Datasets: GSM8K (openai/gsm8k, MIT), MMLU (cais/mmlu, MIT) and the RouteLLM
  evaluation labels (lm-sys/RouteLLM, Apache-2.0) are downloaded by the user
  (scripts/fetch_eval_data.sh) and not redistributed; the repository holds item ids
  and scores only.

- Hugging Face tokenizers corpora: none are bundled.
